   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "בָּא לוֹ לַגּוּף כּוּ׳. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְהֵסִיר אֶת מֻרְאָתוֹ בְּנֹצָתָהּ״ – זוֹ זֶפֶק.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that after the priest throws the bird’s head onto the fire on the altar, «he arrives at the body» and removes the crop and the feathers attached to it and the innards that emerge with them, and tosses them to the place of the ashes. «The Sages taught» in a baraita with regard to the verse pertaining to a bird burnt offering: «“And he shall take away murato with its feathers”» (Leviticus 1:16). «This» word, murato, is referring to the «crop.»"
  }
